00:27:57,279 --> 00:27:59,302
lives in a right sized home,

857
00:27:59,302 --> 00:28:01,325
paid off high interest debt,

858
00:28:01,325 --> 00:28:03,493
takes the full employer match,

859
00:28:03,493 --> 00:28:05,227
and automates investing.

860
00:28:05,407 --> 00:28:07,534
Chris still eats out with friends,

861
00:28:07,534 --> 00:28:08,785
travels once a year,

862
00:28:08,785 --> 00:28:11,224
and doesn't think about coupons at all.

863
00:28:11,574 --> 00:28:12,654
After ten years,

864
00:28:12,654 --> 00:28:14,411
Chris has far more wealth,

865
00:28:14,411 --> 00:28:16,032
and a much happier life.

866
00:28:16,212 --> 00:28:18,253
Pat worked harder at frugality,

867
00:28:18,253 --> 00:28:19,834
but on the wrong things.

868
00:28:20,014 --> 00:28:22,313
That's the lesson of this whole video.

869
00:28:22,493 --> 00:28:23,977
Frugality is about aim,

870
00:28:23,977 --> 00:28:24,687
not effort.

871
00:28:24,867 --> 00:28:26,884
Point your frugal energy at the few

872
00:28:26,884 --> 00:28:29,246
decisions that move thousands of dollars,

873
00:28:29,246 --> 00:28:31,263
and you can stop worrying about the

874
00:28:31,263 --> 00:28:32,588
ones that move pennies.

875
00:28:32,938 --> 00:28:35,666
Frugality looks different depending on your income.

876
00:28:35,846 --> 00:28:37,419
If money is very tight,

877
00:28:37,419 --> 00:28:40,290
the biggest wins are usually avoiding fees

878
00:28:40,290 --> 00:28:41,863
and high interest debt,

879
00:28:41,863 --> 00:28:43,299
using free resources,

880
00:28:43,299 --> 00:28:46,034
and building a small emergency buffer so

881
00:28:46,034 --> 00:28:48,222
surprises don't become new debt.

882
00:28:48,402 --> 00:28:49,509
At low incomes,

883
00:28:49,509 --> 00:28:51,500
small amounts matter a lot,

884
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:53,787
and the money per hour test can

885
00:28:53,787 --> 00:28:55,705
favor smaller savings too.

886
00:28:56,055 --> 00:28:57,315
At middle incomes,

887
00:28:57,315 --> 00:29:00,116
cars and housing are usually the biggest

888
00:29:00,116 --> 00:29:00,606
levers.

889
00:29:00,786 --> 00:29:02,705
A smarter car and a right sized

890
00:29:02,705 --> 00:29:04,934
home can free up hundreds of dollars

891
00:29:04,934 --> 00:29:05,430
a month.

892
00:29:05,610 --> 00:29:08,688
Combined with automatic investing and the full

893
00:29:08,688 --> 00:29:11,365
employer match, this is where many quiet

894
00:29:11,365 --> 00:29:12,838
millionaires are made,

895
00:29:12,838 --> 00:29:14,712
over twenty or thirty years.

896
00:29:15,062 --> 00:29:16,280
At high incomes,

897
00:29:16,280 --> 00:29:18,870
the danger is lifestyle inflation.

898
00:29:19,050 --> 00:29:21,058
Spending rises with every raise,

899
00:29:21,058 --> 00:29:23,442
and many high earners live paycheck to

900
00:29:23,442 --> 00:29:24,007
paycheck.

901
00:29:24,187 --> 00:29:27,252
For them, frugality means keeping fixed costs

902
00:29:27,252 --> 00:29:29,567
well below what they could afford,

903
00:29:29,567 --> 00:29:32,019
saving a large share of every raise,

904
00:29:32,019 --> 00:29:34,880
and keeping investment fees and taxes low.

905
00:29:35,060 --> 00:29:36,430
The habits are the same.

906
00:29:36,610 --> 00:29:37,933
The scale is bigger.

907
00:29:38,283 --> 00:29:40,117
Here's a simple plan for your first

908
00:29:40,117 --> 00:29:40,431
month.

909
00:29:40,611 --> 00:29:42,713
Week one, check your big three.

910
00:29:42,893 --> 00:29:44,249
What do your housing,

911
00:29:44,249 --> 00:29:46,573
car and food really cost each month?

912
00:29:46,753 --> 00:29:48,007
Write the numbers down.

913
00:29:48,187 --> 00:29:50,451
Week two, do the quick wins.

914
00:29:50,631 --> 00:29:52,346
Cancel unused subscriptions,

915
00:29:52,346 --> 00:29:54,428
move your emergency fund to a high

916
00:29:54,428 --> 00:29:57,185
yield account, and confirm you're getting the

917
00:29:57,185 --> 00:29:58,410
full employer match.

918
00:29:58,760 --> 00:30:01,430
Week three, drop one frugal trap.

919
00:30:01,610 --> 00:30:04,502
Stop driving across town for small deals,

920
00:30:04,502 --> 00:30:07,466
or stop buying things just because they're

921
00:30:07,466 --> 00:30:08,030
on sale.

922
00:30:08,210 --> 00:30:09,777
Week four, automate.

923
00:30:09,957 --> 00:30:12,642
Set up an automatic transfer for whatever

924
00:30:12,642 --> 00:30:14,083
money you've freed up,

925
00:30:14,083 --> 00:30:16,506
straight into savings or investments,

926
00:30:16,506 --> 00:30:19,060
so it doesn't drift back into spending.

927
00:30:19,240 --> 00:30:20,178
In thirty days,

928
00:30:20,178 --> 00:30:21,741
you'll have a new system,

929
00:30:21,741 --> 00:30:23,930
and a number that shows it working.

930
00:30:24,281 --> 00:30:25,082
Question one.

931
00:30:25,262 --> 00:30:27,700
Is frugality enough to get rich?

932
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,319
Usually not on its own.

933
00:30:29,499 --> 00:30:31,813
Most people also need to grow their

934
00:30:31,813 --> 00:30:34,259
income over time and invest steadily.

935
00:30:34,439 --> 00:30:37,494
Frugality creates the gap between income and

936
00:30:37,494 --> 00:30:40,478
spending, and investing turns that gap into

937
00:30:40,478 --> 00:30:40,964
wealth.

938
00:30:41,315 --> 00:30:42,197
Question two.

939
00:30:42,377 --> 00:30:44,606
How do I stay frugal without feeling

940
00:30:44,606 --> 00:30:45,163
deprived?

941
00:30:45,343 --> 00:30:46,865
Focus on the big wins,

942
00:30:46,865 --> 00:30:49,632
automate them, and keep spending on what

943
00:30:49,632 --> 00:30:50,254
you love.

944
00:30:50,434 --> 00:30:52,278
When the big decisions are right,

945
00:30:52,278 --> 00:30:54,289
you can relax about the small stuff.

946
00:30:54,639 --> 00:30:55,811
Question three.

947
00:30:55,991 --> 00:30:57,976
What's the first habit to start with?

948
00:30:58,156 --> 00:30:59,563
If you have high interest debt,

949
00:30:59,563 --> 00:31:00,107
start there.

950
00:31:00,287 --> 00:31:02,479
If not, check your car and housing

951
00:31:02,479 --> 00:31:05,058
costs, then automate savings and get the

952
00:31:05,058 --> 00:31:06,347
full employer match.

953
00:31:06,698 --> 00:31:07,661
Question four.

954
00:31:07,841 --> 00:31:10,674
Is it worth buying organic or premium

955
00:31:10,674 --> 00:31:11,057
food?

956
00:31:11,237 --> 00:31:13,334
That's a personal choice and part of

957
00:31:13,334 --> 00:31:14,441
conscious spending.

958
00:31:14,621 --> 00:31:15,905
If it matters to you,

959
00:31:15,905 --> 00:31:18,104
spend there, and cut somewhere else.

960
00:31:18,284 --> 00:31:21,082
Frugality doesn't mean buying the cheapest food.

961
00:31:21,262 --> 00:31:23,737
It means choosing on purpose and wasting

962
00:31:23,737 --> 00:31:25,036
less of what you buy.

963
00:31:25,385 --> 00:31:26,349
Question five.

964
00:31:26,529 --> 00:31:28,526
My partner thinks frugal means cheap.

965
00:31:28,706 --> 00:31:29,867
How do I explain it?

966
00:31:30,047 --> 00:31:32,377
Show the difference between the big wins

967
00:31:32,377 --> 00:31:33,484
and the small cuts.

968
00:31:33,664 --> 00:31:35,769
Most people are happy to drive a

969
00:31:35,769 --> 00:31:37,808
used car if it means a vacation

970
00:31:37,808 --> 00:31:39,585
every year and less stress.

971
00:31:39,765 --> 00:31:42,188
Frugality done right should make your life

972
00:31:42,188 --> 00:31:43,631
feel better, not smaller.

973
00:31:43,811 --> 00:31:46,149
Start with one shared goal and let

974
00:31:46,149 --> 00:31:47,387
the results speak.

975
00:31:47,737 --> 00:31:48,874
Question six.

976
00:31:49,054 --> 00:31:50,384
How do I know if a frugal

977
00:31:50,384 --> 00:31:51,341
habit is worth it?

978
00:31:51,521 --> 00:31:53,832
Use the two questions from this video.

979
00:31:54,012 --> 00:31:55,986
First, how much does it save in

980
00:31:55,986 --> 00:31:58,088
a year, compared with the time it

981
00:31:58,088 --> 00:31:58,470
takes?

982
00:31:58,650 --> 00:32:00,903
Second, does it put my health,

983
00:32:00,903 --> 00:32:03,306
safety or relationships at risk?

984
00:32:03,486 --> 00:32:05,520
If it saves real money for little

985
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:06,568
time and no risk,

986
00:32:06,568 --> 00:32:07,062
keep it.

987
00:32:07,242 --> 00:32:09,436
If not, let it go and focus

988
00:32:09,436 --> 00:32:10,736
on the big wins.

989
00:32:11,087 --> 00:32:11,922
Quick recap.

990
00:32:12,102 --> 00:32:13,751
Angle one, the numbers.

991
00:32:13,931 --> 00:32:15,954
Drive reliable used cars,

992
00:32:15,954 --> 00:32:17,654
right size your home,

993
00:32:17,654 --> 00:32:18,706
cook at home,

994
00:32:18,706 --> 00:32:20,649
kill high interest debt,

995
00:32:20,649 --> 00:32:21,701
pay low fees,

996
00:32:21,701 --> 00:32:25,262
shop insurance, cancel unused subscriptions,

997
00:32:25,262 --> 00:32:26,476
take the match,

998
00:32:26,476 --> 00:32:28,337
use high yield savings,

999
00:32:28,337 --> 00:32:30,766
and buy quality for daily use.

1000
00:32:31,116 --> 00:32:33,252
Angle two, the psychology.

1001
00:32:33,432 --> 00:32:34,430
Ten traps.

1002
00:32:34,610 --> 00:32:36,882
Driving far to save a little,

1003
00:32:36,882 --> 00:32:38,527
wasteful bulk buying,

1004
00:32:38,527 --> 00:32:40,485
skipping preventive care,

1005
00:32:40,485 --> 00:32:41,895
cheap safety gear,

1006
00:32:41,895 --> 00:32:43,775
cheap stuff that breaks,

1007
00:32:43,775 --> 00:32:45,654
cutting all social life,

1008
00:32:45,654 --> 00:32:48,631
extreme couponing, skipping insurance,

1009
00:32:48,631 --> 00:32:51,529
risky DIY, and buying because it's on

1010
00:32:51,529 --> 00:32:51,921
sale.

1011
00:32:52,271 --> 00:32:53,942
Angle three, the playbook.

1012
00:32:54,122 --> 00:32:57,342
Automate savings, use a waiting rule,

1013
00:32:57,342 --> 00:32:59,256
think in cost per use,

1014
00:32:59,256 --> 00:33:01,257
spend on what you love,

1015
00:33:01,257 --> 00:33:02,824
use sinking funds,

1016
00:33:02,824 --> 00:33:04,477
audit bills yearly,

1017
00:33:04,477 --> 00:33:07,174
plan meals, use free resources,

1018
00:33:07,174 --> 00:33:10,133
negotiate, and invest the savings.

1019
00:33:10,483 --> 00:33:12,224
Remember Pat and Chris.

1020
00:33:12,404 --> 00:33:14,557
Same effort, very different results,

1021
00:33:14,557 --> 00:33:16,530
because one aimed at the big wins

1022
00:33:16,530 --> 00:33:18,383
and the other aimed at pennies.

1023
00:33:18,563 --> 00:33:21,524
Frugality done right isn't about being cheap.

1024
00:33:21,704 --> 00:33:23,283
It's about being free.

1025
00:33:23,463 --> 00:33:25,659
Pick one habit from angle one,

1026
00:33:25,659 --> 00:33:27,782
drop one trap from angle two,

1027
00:33:27,782 --> 00:33:30,125
and set up one system from angle

1028
00:33:30,125 --> 00:33:31,369
three this month.

1029
00:33:31,549 --> 00:33:32,941
If you want the full plan,

1030
00:33:32,941 --> 00:33:34,012
it's in my playbook,

1031
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:35,404
linked in the description.

1032
00:33:35,584 --> 00:33:37,551
Tell me in the comments your favorite

1033
00:33:37,551 --> 00:33:38,242
frugal habit.

1034
00:33:38,422 --> 00:33:39,676
I'm Ryan Rover.

1035
00:33:39,856 --> 00:33:41,006
See you in the next one.
